# Build context for the service images (docker build -f services/<name>/Dockerfile .).
# Allowlist: the Dockerfiles copy only the root pom.xml, each service's pom.xml
# and the service's own directory, so send nothing else. Without this, every
# build uploads frontend/node_modules, infra/ and all target/ directories.
*
!pom.xml
!services/*/pom.xml
!services/*/src/
# Lombok reads these at compile time: without engagement-service's, @Value is
# not copied onto its constructors and the service fails to start.
!services/*/lombok.config
# The shared gRPC contracts (ADR-0021): user-service generates its auditor
# client from them, and the auditor its server.
!proto/
# The auditor is a Go module, so its build also needs these.
!services/auditor/go.mod
!services/auditor/go.sum
**/target/
# Mockery's output (git-ignored) is for tests only, and a stale copy left in a
# working tree would not compile. Not mocks_*.go: client-profile names its
# generated ORM files that way, and its image needs them.
**/mocks.go
